### 2. The `ProductCard` Component
This is the core component. It's a functional component that accepts `image`, `title`, and `price` as props.

**`src/components/ProductCard.js`**
```jsx
import React from 'react';
import './ProductCard.css';

/**
 * A reusable component to display a product card.
 *
 * @param {object} props - The properties for the component.
 * @param {string} props.image - The URL of the product image.
 * @param {string} props.title - The title or name of the product.
 * @param {number} props.price - The price of the product.
 */
const ProductCard = ({ image, title, price }) => {
  // Format the price to a currency string (e.g., 29.99 -> $29.99)
  const formattedPrice = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {
    style: 'currency',
    currency: 'USD',
  }).format(price);

  return (
    <div className="product-card">
      <img src={image} alt={title} className="product-image" />
      <div className="product-info">
        <h3 className="product-title">{title}</h3>
        <p className="product-price">{formattedPrice}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};

export default ProductCard;
```

#### Key Features:
*   **Props Destructuring:** We use `{ image, title, price }` in the function signature to directly access the props.
*   **Reusable & Dumb:** The component only knows how to display the data it's given. It doesn't manage its own state, making it highly reusable.
*   **Price Formatting:** Using `Intl.NumberFormat` is the modern, recommended way to format currency, as it handles internationalization and locale-specific formatting correctly.
*   **CSS Import:** We import a dedicated CSS file for styling.

